# QuickNotes System Design

QuickNotes is moving from a browser-only app to an online service for 1 million users. This repository has two parts:

1. **API client:** a small HTML/CSS/JavaScript page that loads, creates and deletes notes using the [JSONPlaceholder](https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com) practice API.
2. **Design documents:** the real API, data model and architecture for the backend team.

## How to run the API client

1. Clone the repository: `git clone https://github.com/your-username/quicknotes-system-design.git`
2. Open `index.html` in a browser (double-click it, or run `python3 -m http.server` and visit `http://localhost:8000`).
3. Click **Load notes** to fetch 10 notes, use the form to add a note, and click **Delete** on a note to remove it.

No build step or installation is needed. Note: JSONPlaceholder pretends to save changes but does not store them, so created notes disappear when you reload.

